% The beetle is a green or blue car. Green things are nice or pretty, and
% both blue and pretty things are beautiful. Cars cannot be beautiful, so
% the beetle must be green and must be nice.
% Shows disjunctive conclusions and the elimination of impossible alternatives.
% See https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disjunctive_syllogism

the templates are:
    *a thing* is a car,
    *a thing* has property *a property*,
    *a thing* has property *a first property* or *a second property*,
    *a property* entails *a consequence*,
    *a property* entails *a first property* or *a second property*,
    *a thing* cannot have property *a property*,
    *a thing* is nice.

the knowledge base beetle alternatives includes:
beetle is a car.

% The two properties in a disjunctive conclusion remain alternatives.
a car has property green or blue
    if the car is a car.

green entails nice or pretty.
pretty entails beautiful.
blue entails beautiful.

a car cannot have property beautiful
    if the car is a car.

% A property is impossible when it entails another impossible property.
a thing cannot have property a property
    if the property entails a consequence
    and the thing cannot have property the consequence.

% Either alternative follows when its counterpart is impossible.
a thing has property a property
    if the thing has property a property or an excluded property
    and the thing cannot have property the excluded property.

a thing has property a property
    if the thing has property an excluded property or a property
    and the thing cannot have property the excluded property.

% A property that has been established can give further alternatives.
a thing has property a first property or a second property
    if the thing has property a known property
    and the known property entails the first property or the second property.

a thing is nice
    if the thing has property nice.

query nice is:
    beetle is nice.

query properties is:
    beetle has property which property.
